{#
    formSection(id, eyebrow, title, headingLevel, classes)
    - Narrow, centered section for a single form (or any other narrow-column content) — same
      reading-width treatment as articleContent()'s .c-article__inner. Distinct from
      contentSection()'s 2/3+1/3 reading-column + sidebar layout, which doesn't fit a single
      centered form.
    - Body is a freeform call block, e.g. matchForm() today — but any other form (or narrow
      content) can reuse this same section shell:
      {% call formSection(eyebrow="Doporučeno na míru", title="Najdeme vám ideální klub, hernu nebo trenéra") %}
          {{ matchForm(...) }}
      {% endcall %}
    - headingLevel: "h2" (default) | "h3"
    - Header/eyebrow/title reuse the generic .c-section__* elements (section.css) instead of
      component-specific ones — this shell has nothing distinctive enough to warrant its own.
#}
{% macro formSection(
    id="",
    eyebrow="",
    title="",
    headingLevel="h2",
    classes=""
) %}
<section{% if id %} id="{{ id }}"{% endif %} class="{{ ["c-section", "c-section--form", classes] | select | join(" ") }}">
    <div class="c-container c-section__inner">
        <header class="c-section__header">
            {% if eyebrow %}<p class="c-section__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
            <{{ headingLevel }} class="c-section__title">{{ title }}</{{ headingLevel }}>
        </header>
        {{ caller() }}
    </div>
</section>
{% endmacro %}
